      "cooked": "<p><div class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"><a class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/original/2X/e/e785eecd7966c4405653d9ac713b6f90229efa74.jpeg\" data-download-href=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/e785eecd7966c4405653d9ac713b6f90229efa74\" title=\"20230109225334_1\"><img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/e/e785eecd7966c4405653d9ac713b6f90229efa74_2_690x388.jpeg\" alt=\"20230109225334_1\" data-base62-sha1=\"x29fdpd140Ig70dV1Epc1kpyosc\" width=\"690\" height=\"388\" srcset=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/e/e785eecd7966c4405653d9ac713b6f90229efa74_2_690x388.jpeg, https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/e/e785eecd7966c4405653d9ac713b6f90229efa74_2_1035x582.jpeg 1.5x, https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/e/e785eecd7966c4405653d9ac713b6f90229efa74_2_1380x776.jpeg 2x\" data-small-upload=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/uploads/default/optimized/2X/e/e785eecd7966c4405653d9ac713b6f90229efa74_2_10x10.png\"><div class=\"meta\">\n<svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#far-image\"></use></svg><span class=\"filename\">20230109225334_1</span><span class=\"informations\">1920×1080 380 KB</span><svg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#discourse-expand\"></use></svg>\n</div></a></div></p>\n<p>Friction, Fright Train, and the Operative crash the set at Champion Studios! Tachyon &amp; Bunker in their Freedom Five suits, along with Mr. Fixer, show up just in time to take them right into the danger zone!*</p>\n<p>*Danger level may vary. Not very much in my case, but I definitely felt the need for speed! I think it ended by the start of the 4th environment turn. Tachyon stepped up to the plate, took a swing, and knocked the Operative over the fence! Strike three, they’re out!</p>\n<p>Now please excuse me while I go sort out my mixed metaphors.</p>",
